			<div class="content" id="post-content-1356601">
									

<p>Bacteriostatic means that it stops bacteria from reproducing. this includes, the erythromycin groups, the two medications in Bactrim/Septra, and the tetracycline group. These would probably not help very much, since this is such an aggressive infection, and the immune system is being damaged.</p>
<p>Bacteriocidal agents kill bacteria. These antibiotics include the penicillins, cephalosporins, fluoroquinolones, vancomycin and others. These might have some benefit. Alcohol is also bacteriocidal, as well as iodine and many others.</p>

